### add_controlrig_rigvm_links

Add reviewed ControlRig RigVM links on a sample/temp ControlRig Blueprint.

**Important scope note:** this command is a guarded writer. It refuses targets
outside `/Game/_MCP_Sample` and `/Game/_MCP_Temp`, validates every requested
link before mutation, treats already-linked specs as idempotent success, and
only then calls `URigVMController::AddLink`. It does not create cast nodes,
modify original/engine ControlRig assets, execute, solve, or write runtime code.
Use `validate_controlrig_rigvm_links` first when planning links for non-temp
assets.

**Parameters:**
- `control_rig_path`, `control_rig_asset_path`, or `control_rig` (string, optional) - Sample/temp ControlRig Blueprint asset path or generated class path.
- `control_rig_class_path` or `control_rig_class` (string, optional) - Generated ControlRig class path. The owning asset must still be under sample/temp roots.
- `links` (array, optional) - Link specs with `source_pin_path`/`from` and `target_pin_path`/`to`, or strings in `Source -> Target` form.
- `unit_links` (array, optional) - Alias for `links`, intended for reviewed unit-link specs.
- `allow_type_casting` or `enable_type_casting` (boolean, optional) - Allow type casting during feasibility checks. Defaults to `false`; cast-node creation is still disabled.
- `dry_run` or `validate_only` (boolean, optional) - Validate and report `will_add_link` without mutation.
- `compile` (boolean, optional) - Compile/reinitialize after successful mutation. Defaults to `true`.
- `save_asset` or `save` (boolean, optional) - Save only the target sample/temp ControlRig asset. Defaults to `false`.
- `max_links` (integer, optional) - Maximum link specs to process. Defaults to `64`, clamped to `256`.

**Returns:**
- `sample_only=true`, target path, dirty-state guards, `target_modified`, compile/save result
- `compile_succeeded`, `save_succeeded`, and `completion_errors`; top-level
  `success` is false when requested compile/save fails or any requested link
  cannot be applied
- `partial_target_modified=true` when one or more links were applied before a
  later link failed
- per-link validation plus `will_add_link`, `writer_candidate`, and `applied`
- aggregate `would_add_count`, `links_added_count`, missing/already-linked/can-link counts, and graph link counts before/after

**Example:**
```json
{
  "command": "add_controlrig_rigvm_links",
  "params": {
    "control_rig_path": "/Game/_MCP_Temp/ControlRigWriterSmoke/CR_AddControlCopy",
    "links": [
      {
        "from": "VariableNode.Value",
        "to": "ParentConstraint_1.bMaintainOffset"
      }
    ],
    "dry_run": true
  }
}
```

### set_controlrig_rigvm_pin_defaults

Set reviewed ControlRig RigVM pin defaults on a sample/temp ControlRig
Blueprint.

**Important scope note:** this command is a guarded writer. It refuses targets
outside `/Game/_MCP_Sample` and `/Game/_MCP_Temp`, requires every pin spec to
include a proposed value, validates every requested default before mutation, and
only then calls `URigVMController::SetPinDefaultValue`. By default it does not
resize arrays or propagate values to linked pins. It does not modify
original/engine ControlRig assets, execute, solve, or write runtime code. Use
`validate_controlrig_rigvm_pin_defaults` first when planning defaults for
non-temp assets.

**Parameters:**
- `control_rig_path`, `control_rig_asset_path`, or `control_rig` (string, optional) - Sample/temp ControlRig Blueprint asset path or generated class path.
- `control_rig_class_path` or `control_rig_class` (string, optional) - Generated ControlRig class path. The owning asset must still be under sample/temp roots.
- `pin_defaults` (array, optional) - Pin specs with `pin_path`/`pin`/`path` and `default_value`/`value`/`default`.
- `defaults` (array, optional) - Alias for `pin_defaults`.
- `resize_arrays` (boolean, optional) - Permit RigVM array resize while setting defaults. Defaults to `false`.
- `set_value_on_linked_pins` (boolean, optional) - Propagate to linked pins. Defaults to `false`.
- `dry_run` or `validate_only` (boolean, optional) - Validate and report `will_set_default` without mutation.
- `compile` (boolean, optional) - Compile/reinitialize after successful mutation. Defaults to `true`.
- `save_asset` or `save` (boolean, optional) - Save only the target sample/temp ControlRig asset. Defaults to `false`.
- `max_pins` (integer, optional) - Maximum pin specs to process. Defaults to `64`, clamped to `512`.

**Returns:**
- `sample_only=true`, target path, dirty-state guards, `target_modified`, compile/save result
- `compile_succeeded`, `save_succeeded`, and `completion_errors`; top-level
  `success` is false when requested compile/save fails or any requested default
  cannot be applied
- `partial_target_modified=true` when one or more defaults were set before a
  later default failed
- per-pin validation plus `already_matching`, `will_set_default`, `writer_candidate`, `applied`, and default readback after mutation
- aggregate `would_set_count`, `defaults_set_count`, missing/default-capable/proposed-valid counts, and idempotent already-matching count

**Example:**
```json
{
  "command": "set_controlrig_rigvm_pin_defaults",
  "params": {
    "control_rig_path": "/Game/_MCP_Temp/ControlRigWriterSmoke/CR_AddControlCopy",
    "pin_defaults": [
      {
        "pin_path": "ParentConstraint_1.bMaintainOffset",
        "value": "False"
      }
    ],
    "dry_run": true
  }
}
```

### ensure_controlrig_sample_asset

Create or reuse a sample-only ControlRig Blueprint asset.

**Important scope note:** this command refuses target paths outside
`/Game/_MCP_Sample` and `/Game/_MCP_Temp`. It creates a ControlRig Blueprint,
optionally assigns a preview SkeletalMesh, optionally imports a bounded preview
hierarchy from a read-only SkeletalMesh/Skeleton, optionally adds bounded
direct hierarchy curves, local/global transform nulls, or direct
float/bool/euler transform controls, or bounded allowlisted single-instance
ControlRig event RigVM unit node evidence, compiles or initializes the target, optionally saves only the target,
and reads back the generated class, preview mesh, hierarchy import evidence,
direct curve evidence, direct null evidence, direct control evidence, and
bounded RigVM unit-node evidence. Direct
null/control objects may include `parent` or `parent_name` as a string resolved
to an existing/imported or earlier direct Bone/Null/Control hierarchy key. It
also supports `transform`, `global_transform`, or `local_transform` on direct
null objects. Direct control objects may include `shape_name`, `shape_color`, or
`shape_transform` metadata. Direct transform controls use
`control_type="transform"` or `control_type="euler_transform"` and accept
transform defaults only through `value`, `default_value`, `initial_value`, or
`default`. `unit_nodes` accepts only `begin_execution`,
`pre_begin_execution`, `post_begin_execution`, `prepare_for_execution`,
`post_prepare_for_execution`, and `inverse_execution` event units with optional
`name`/`node_name` and `position`/`graph_position`; UE 5.6.1 public headers do
not expose `FRigUnit_EndExecution`, so this command does not synthesize an
unavailable end unit or create links. It does not directly author control transform fields,
proxy/channel controls, animation channels, arbitrary RigVM script structs,
unit links, variables, functions, comments, reroutes, dispatch nodes, exposed
pins, or graph replacement.

**Parameters:**
- `target_control_rig_path` (string, required) - Target sample ControlRig package path.
- `skeletal_mesh_path` (string, optional) - Read-only SkeletalMesh used as preview input when no explicit preview mesh is supplied.
- `skeleton_path` (string, optional) - Read-only Skeleton used only for validation.
- `preview_skeletal_mesh_path` (string, optional) - Explicit preview mesh override.
- `setup_mode` (string, optional) - `empty`, `empty_with_preview`, or `import_preview_hierarchy`. Defaults to `empty_with_preview`.
- `curves` (array, optional) - Direct sample hierarchy curves as strings or objects with `name` and optional `value`.
- `nulls` (array, optional) - Direct sample nulls as strings or objects with `name`, optional string `parent`/`parent_name`, and optional `transform`, `global_transform`, or `local_transform` object. Parents resolve only to existing/imported or earlier direct Bone/Null/Control keys.
- `controls` (array, optional) - Direct sample controls as strings or objects with `name`, optional `control_type` (`float`, `bool`, `transform`, or `euler_transform`), optional `value`/`default_value`/`initial_value`/`default`, optional string `parent`/`parent_name`, and optional `shape_name`, `shape_color`, or `shape_transform`. Strings become float controls with default `0.0`. Transform controls use UE `ERigControlType::EulerTransform`; their value fields must be transform objects with `translation`/`location`, `rotation`, or `scale`/`scale3d`. Parents resolve only to existing/imported or earlier direct Bone/Null/Control keys. `shape_color` accepts `[r,g,b,a?]` or `{r,g,b,a}` with components in `0..1` or `0..255`; `shape_transform` accepts a transform object.
- `unit_nodes` (array, optional) - Bounded RigVM unit nodes as strings or objects. Only single-instance public ControlRig event units are accepted: `begin_execution`, `pre_begin_execution`, `post_begin_execution`, `prepare_for_execution`, `post_prepare_for_execution`, and `inverse_execution`; aliases such as `Forwards Solve`, `Pre Forwards Solve`, `Post Forwards Solve`, `Construction`, `PostConstruction`, and `Backwards Solve` are accepted. Object fields are limited to `type`/`unit_type`/`unit`/`kind`, optional `name`/`node_name`, and optional `position`/`graph_position` as `[x, y]` or `{x, y}`.
- `max_direct_curves` (integer, optional) - Maximum direct curve entries accepted. Defaults to `32`, clamped to `128`.
- `max_direct_nulls` (integer, optional) - Maximum direct null entries accepted. Defaults to `32`, clamped to `128`.
- `max_direct_controls` (integer, optional) - Maximum direct control entries accepted. Defaults to `32`, clamped to `128`.
- `max_unit_nodes` (integer, optional) - Maximum RigVM unit node entries accepted. Defaults to `6`, clamped to `6`.
- `allow_existing_target_reuse` (boolean, optional) - Reuse an existing sample ControlRig. Defaults to `true`.
- `overwrite_existing` (boolean, optional) - Delete and recreate the target sample ControlRig. Defaults to `false`.
- `modular_rig` (boolean, optional) - Create a modular rig instead of a standard ControlRig. Defaults to `false`.
- `compile` (boolean, optional) - Compile/initialize after creation or preview assignment. Defaults to `true`.
- `save_asset` or `save` (boolean, optional) - Save the target sample ControlRig. Defaults to `false`.
- `dry_run` or `validate_only` (boolean, optional) - Validate without creating, editing, compiling, or saving.

**Returns:**
- `source_modified=false`, `sample_only=true`, target create/reuse flags
- `control_rig_class_path`, `preview_skeletal_mesh_readback`
- `hierarchy_import` with source type, bounded bone/curve key readback, counts, and truncation flag when `setup_mode=import_preview_hierarchy`
- `direct_curves` with requested curve specs, added curve keys, counts, and truncation flag when `curves` is supplied
- `direct_nulls` with requested null specs, added null keys, parent key and transform readback when applicable, counts, identity/root-level flags, and truncation flag when `nulls` is supplied
- `direct_controls` with requested control specs, added control keys, parent key readback, transform value readback when applicable, shape metadata readback when applicable, counts, root-level/scalar/transform/shape customization flags, and truncation flag when `controls` is supplied
- `rigvm_summary` with requested unit specs, allowed-unit scope, node add/reuse counts, node title/event/script struct readback, pin readback, and explicit unsupported link/arbitrary-struct flags when `unit_nodes` is supplied
- `can_create_transient_control_rig`, `compile_result`, `target_asset_saved`
- `compile_succeeded`, `save_succeeded`, and `completion_errors`; top-level
  `success` is false when requested compile or save fails
- error responses after target preparation include `partial_target_modified`,
  target create/reuse flags, and `target_dirty_after`
- dirty-state guards for source Skeleton/SkeletalMesh/preview mesh inputs

**Example:**
```json
{
  "command": "ensure_controlrig_sample_asset",
  "params": {
    "target_control_rig_path": "/Game/_MCP_Temp/AnimControlRigSmoke/CR_MCP_Sample",
    "skeletal_mesh_path": "/Game/Characters/Bot/SKM_Bot.SKM_Bot",
    "setup_mode": "import_preview_hierarchy",
    "curves": [{"name": "MCP_TestGate", "value": 1.0}],
    "nulls": [
      {"name": "MCP_RootNull", "global_transform": {"translation": [0, 0, 50]}},
      {"name": "MCP_AimNull", "parent": "MCP_RootNull", "local_transform": {"translation": [25, 0, 0]}}
    ],
    "controls": [
      {
        "name": "MCP_FKAlpha",
        "control_type": "float",
        "value": 0.5,
        "parent": "MCP_AimNull",
        "shape_name": "Circle",
        "shape_color": [0.2, 0.6, 1.0, 1.0],
        "shape_transform": {"translation": [0, 0, 5], "scale": [1.5, 1.5, 1.5]}
      },
      {
        "name": "MCP_WorldControl",
        "control_type": "transform",
        "value": {"translation": [10, 20, 30], "rotation": [0, 45, 0], "scale": [1, 1, 1]},
        "parent": "MCP_AimNull",
        "shape_name": "Box"
      }
    ],
    "unit_nodes": [
      {"type": "prepare_for_execution", "name": "MCP_Construction", "position": [-360, -160]},
      {"type": "begin_execution", "name": "MCP_BeginExecution", "position": [-280, 0]}
    ],
    "compile": true,
    "save_asset": false
  }
}
```

**UE 5.6.1 smoke fixture:**

This repository has verified creation under
`/Game/_MCP_Temp/AnimControlRigSmoke/CR_MCP_Sample` with preview mesh
`/Engine/Tutorial/SubEditors/TutorialAssets/Character/TutorialTPP.TutorialTPP`.
The command produced
`/Game/_MCP_Temp/AnimControlRigSmoke/CR_MCP_Sample.CR_MCP_Sample_C`, compiled
successfully, created a transient ControlRig instance, and cleaned up with no
dirty source packages.

The same command has also been verified as an upstream step for
`ensure_anim_graph_controlrig_node_sample`: a generated sample ControlRig class
from `/Game/_MCP_Temp/AnimControlRigE2E/CR_MCP_E2E` compiled successfully when
bound into `/Game/_MCP_Temp/AnimControlRigE2E/ABP_MCP_ControlRigE2E`, then both
temp assets were deleted with no dirty packages left.

